course: dictionary
lesson: 1220
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word building is a good example. «A howler monkey booms so loud it fills the building.» Here a building is a structure with walls and a roof, so the monkey's noise fills a real place.
explain: Now read this: «Sleep isn't a break from training, it is the part of training where the body does its building.» A building here is not a place at all. It means making something, like making muscles stronger. Ask yourself: is it a thing or an action? The words around the word give you the answer.
explain: Building can also be a verb, a doing word. «We are building a den» means we are putting parts together to make it. The -ing ending tells you the action is happening now. Swap in another verb like making; if the sentence still fits, you have the right meaning.
fact: A building is a structure with walls and a roof, such as a house, school, shop or church.
fact: Building can mean the work of making houses and other structures: «building is hard work».
fact: As a verb, building means making something by putting parts together: «we are building a den».
fact: Safety: «Once you are out of a burning building, you never go back inside, not even for a pet or a toy.»
fact: «Lincoln Cathedral in England was probably the tallest building in the world for about 200 years, until its spire fell in 1548.»
exercise: «Once you are out of a burning building, you never go back inside.» What does building mean here? | *A structure with walls and a roof | Putting parts together to make a den | A pile of bricks on a field | The work of making houses
exercise: Jake says, «Building is hard work.» What does building mean in this sentence? | *The work of making houses and other structures | Putting parts together to make a den | Shouting very loudly | A tall structure with a roof
exercise: «We are building a den.» What kind of word is building here? | A noun, naming a place | A question word | An adjective, describing a den | *A verb, showing an action
test: «The howler monkey booms so loud it fills the building.» What does building mean in this sentence? | Putting parts together | *A structure with walls and a roof | The work of making a house | A tree in the zoo
test: «Sleep is the part of training where the body does its building.» What does building mean here? | Walking home from school | A tall structure with a roof | *Making something new, like stronger muscles | Drawing pictures on paper
exam: Maya says building always means a house. Is she right? | No, it means a tree | *No, it can also mean a school, shop or church, or the act of making things | Yes, but only in the summer | Yes, building only ever means a house
